#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
"""support: collect, load and query nano support bundles.

  support collect [--install-dir ~/nano | --ssh USER@HOST | --kubernetes] [--since 24h]
                  [--no-probes] [--out-dir DIR] [--yes]
  support load BUNDLE [BUNDLE...] [--replace]
  support query "SQL" [--format PrettyCompact]     (or @file.sql, or - for stdin)
  support shell
  support status
  support down
  support check BUNDLE                              (scan a bundle for secret-looking text)

collect wraps nano's own support bundle tool (scripts/nano support-bundle) from
YOUR install, so the version always matches your release and its redaction is
the one nano ships. Optional live probes (health, migrations, Vector restarts
and topology, ClickHouse parts, merges, mutations, errors and query_log totals
with no query text, PostgreSQL pg_stat summaries, disk and memory) go through
that same redaction. Nothing is written until you have seen a preview and said
yes. Nothing is uploaded, ever: you decide where the file goes.

load starts a throwaway ClickHouse in Docker on 127.0.0.1 (random port, random
password in a 0600 file), parses the bundle into tables (logs, k8s_events,
facts, probes) and prints starter queries. down removes it and its data.

Python 3.9+ standard library only. Docker is needed for load/query/shell.
"""
